{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe journey has been a mixture of damp and discovery. I spent a day in Koblenz, waiting for Councillor Lange who never showed, which left me with nothing but my thoughts and the rain. On Wednesday I took a boat to Neuwied and visited the Moravian Sisters’ House; there is a quiet dignity in their order that one rarely finds these days.\n\nThe river has been unkind, and I am soaked through from the journey to Linz. I stopped there to see a painting Schulze mentioned in a hilltop church. It is competent, though not profound. At Bonn, I called on Windischmann and his son-in-law Walther. We discussed the state of affairs in the Rhineland, and I found the men eager, if somewhat confused about their own position in history.\n\nI am tired, but the wine here is excellent. I miss your company and the calm of our home. Do not worry for me; I am merely wet, not ill.\n\nYour affectionate\nGeorg"}}],"created":1795080204,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":217,"prompt_tokens":952,"total_tokens":1169,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-PuFSJQ4tK46jWlv36q8t1itfaT6WLZVO","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":952,"prompt_ms":914.404,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9605084033613446,"prompt_per_second":1041.115305707324,"predicted_n":217,"predicted_ms":5197.015,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.060254629629632,"predicted_per_second":41.56231990863986}}